<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Stari Grad</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Pharos (Hvar)</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Stari Grad is a town on the Croatian island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hvar">Hvar</a>. It was founded in 384 BCE as Pharos by Greek colonists from the island of Paros, who defeated the local <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/illyrians">Illyrians</a> with help from Syracuse. Pharos became a centre of Greek life in the Adriatic and was later ruled by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/demetrius-of-pharos">Demetrius of Pharos</a>. The surrounding Stari Grad Plain, whose ancient Greek field divisions survive, is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>.</p></div>
